\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Thou whose hand hath 
\par brought us
\par Unto this joyful day,
\par Accept our glad thanksgiving,
\par And listen as we pray;
\par And may our preparation
\par For this day's service be
\par With one accord to offer
\par Ourselves, O Lord, to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For this new house we praise Thee,
\par Reared at Thine own command,
\par For every generous bosom,
\par And every willing Thy temple
\par And now within Thy temple
\par Thy glory let us see,
\par For all its strength  and beauty
\par Are nothing without Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And oft as here we gather,
\par And hearts in worship blend,
\par May truth reveal its power,
\par And fervent prayer ascend;
\par Here may the busy toiler
\par Rise to the things above,
\par The young, the old, be strengthened,
\par And all men learn Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And as the years roll onward,
\par And strong affections twine,
\par And tender memories gather
\par About this sacred shrine,
\par May this its chiefest honour,
\par Its glory, ever be,
\par That multitudes within it
\par Have found their way to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord God, our father's helper,
\par Our joy, and hope, and stay,
\par Grant now a gracious earnest
\par Of many a coming day.
\par Our yearning hearts Thou knowest;
\par We wait before Thou throne:
\par O come, and by Thy prsence
\par Make this new house Thine own.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

